WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.611
SidePulse Dot

00:00:01.871 --> 00:00:03.262
a tiny USB-C

00:00:03.074 --> 00:00:03.581
light

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.595
Peter Kuhar's SidePulse

00:00:05.419 --> 00:00:06.138
Dot is a

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.449
3D-printed USB-C plug

00:00:08.285 --> 00:00:09.628
with two programmable

00:00:09.452 --> 00:00:11.126
RGB LEDs that

00:00:10.938 --> 00:00:12.152
shows whether Claude

00:00:11.964 --> 00:00:13.107
or Codex agents

00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:13.638
are working

00:00:13.851 --> 00:00:14.911
need input or

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:15.607
are done on

00:00:15.419 --> 00:00:16.114
a Mac

00:00:16.654 --> 00:00:17.797
On an iPhone

00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:18.906
the CLI sends

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:19.920
an animation as

00:00:19.732 --> 00:00:21.123
a push notification

00:00:20.935 --> 00:00:21.854
to the SidePulse

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:22.137
app

00:00:22.232 --> 00:00:23.257
which forwards it

00:00:23.069 --> 00:00:23.800
to the Dot

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.896
over USB-C

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.128
It costs $29

00:00:27.211 --> 00:00:30.029
discounted to $19.72

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:30.866
for Black Friday

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:31.668
and is a

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.458
first batch for

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:33.201
enthusiasts

00:00:33.272 --> 00:00:34.816
a larger 8-LED

00:00:34.628 --> 00:00:36.019
SidePulse Pro fits

00:00:35.831 --> 00:00:36.927
the MacBook Pro

00:00:36.751 --> 00:00:37.741
SD slot

00:00:38.262 --> 00:00:39.276
Full story on

00:00:39.087 --> 00:00:39.983
the dashboard
